.envrc
runbin/
autoplay10.txt
qasweep.txt
sweep-balance.json

# C6 SHIPS LIKE A PRODUCT — this block reached `main` as an UNRESOLVED MERGE CONFLICT: commit
# 17934ee's .gitignore literally contained `<<<<<<< HEAD` / `=======` / `>>>>>>> wave/first-hour`
# as committed lines. Git read them as three harmless patterns, so nothing ever failed and no
# self-test could see it — but it is the first file a stranger opens after README, and the wave
# whose job is "what does a stranger receive" is the right one to fix it. Both sides are kept.
#
# W4 THE BOARD BECOMES A PLACE — the BOARDTEST pixel probe's frame + that wave's shell helpers
sightline_boardtest.png
.w4*.sh
bal/
# W9 THE REPAIR — wave-local scratch. Kept SHORT and wave-scoped on purpose: generic names
# (t.sh / sweep.sh / frames.sh ...) would shadow a real project file later, so the wave's throwaway
# scripts are deleted from the worktree rather than ignored forever.
.w9*
# Every agent is told to point SIGHTLINE_BALANCE_JSON at $PWD/balance.json (see the dev contract),
# so this one is durable, not wave-local — it belongs beside sweep-balance.json above.
balance.json
.w9s/
.w9exit.sh
.w9gate.sh
.w9t.sh
.w9shot.sh
.w9sweep.sh
.w9rev.md
